From 483429f99b3978d565629738bcac5227017834a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moto <j3tm0t0@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:39:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] SD card: HDS files on an SPI SD card ("sd:/path.hds" in an
 HDS slot), opt-in; one-time fetch from the share

A config HDS entry starting with "sd:" opens that file on a microSD card wired to SPI0
(GP18 SCK / GP19 MOSI / GP20 MISO / GP21 CS, 25 MHz; SD_SCK/SD_MOSI/SD_MISO/SD_CS/SD_SPI_HZ),
via no-OS-FatFS-SD-SDIO-SPI-RPi-Pico (lib/FatFs_SD). Port of sdhds 6db6256. Such a disk does
not wait for Wi-Fi; ID 0 / BOOTWAIT / ID 6 are unchanged.

Opt-in only: an extra SCSI ID is given a drive letter at boot before CONFIG.SYS drivers, so
e.g. HDS1 = "sd:/x68000z/hds1.hds" takes B: and the remote drive moves to C:.

After the first connect, if the card has no /x68000z/hds1.hds and the HDS0 share has
sdcopy/hds1.hds, it is copied onto the card once (.part, then rename). Copying does not
enable it; HDS1 still has to name it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
